;; re-frame2 event-conformance tier — the broader event-conformance TEST
;; surface (rf2-xhfxcs.6; EP-0018 §Conformance + Bead Plan item 7).
;;
;; Its CORE lock is the EP-0018 one-form event-MODEL contract (the
;; `event_model_conformance_cljs_test.cljc` umbrella), but follow-on locks
;; have since landed alongside it on this same surface:
;;
;;   - the EP-0017 recordable-coeffect locks live IN the model-conformance
;;     ns (flat declared delivery, the one-arg ambient supplier arg path,
;;     and the slice-B recordable-generator / mint-policy machinery —
;;     `:live` mint + write-back, `:strict` refuse-to-mint, `:explicit-live`
;;     escape; rf2-lpyw1v); and
;;   - the EP-0023 image-loaded frame dispatch-isolation lock is a SEPARATE
;;     ns (`event_frame_isolation_conformance_cljs_test.cljc`, rf2-slvzn3)
;;     this alias also runs.
;;
;; This is NOT a published Maven artefact — it has no `src/`. It is a
;; cross-artefact TEST surface (the precedent is `reply-conformance/` and
;; `derivation-conformance/`) that holds the umbrella REGRESSION LOCK on
;; the one-form event-registration PUBLIC CONTRACT EP-0018 settled:
;;
;;   - `reg-event` is the SINGLE public event-registration form, with
;;     reg-event-fx semantics (coeffects in / a closed effects map out;
;;     `{:db …}` is the db-write effect; `:rf.cofx/requires` works
;;     uniformly — the EP-0017 hole closed).
;;   - the THREE retired public names (`reg-event-db` / `reg-event-fx` /
;;     `reg-event-ctx`) survive ONLY as facade-exported `^:no-doc`
;;     throwing stubs that raise their exact hard errors
;;     (`:rf.error/reg-event-{db,fx,ctx}-removed`) — production-survivable
;;     (fan out on the always-on error channel, THEN throw).
;;   - ONE unified `:rf/event-handler` wrapper (`:rf/default? true`); the
;;     `:event/kind` sub-tag is GONE; `reg-event-ctx` is NOT a public
;;     (doc'd) facade var.
;;
;; This tier carries NO realm-routing / frame-query section. The EP-0013
;; multi-realm substrate was retired in the EP-0023/EP-0024 realm collapse
;; (rf2-afdlyr / rf2-tu2vr7) — there is no public realm query coordinate;
;; the public read grammar is FRAME-TARGETED over a live frame's sealed
;; image generation. The frame/query read contract (`rf/handler-meta` /
;; `rf/registrations` `{:frame …}`) is locked in core's
;; `re-frame.facade-frame-read-cljs-test`, and the live-dispatch isolation
;; leg in the sibling `re-frame.event-frame-isolation-conformance-cljs-test`
;; — not restated here.
;;
;; ## Ownership split — what core owns, what this tier owns
;;
;; The BASELINE reg-event unit behaviour is owned by core's
;; `re-frame.reg-event-cljs-test` (registration shape, `:db`/`:fx` effect
;; semantics, nil/{} no-op, `:rf.cofx/requires` flat delivery + storage,
;; the retired-name stubs, the reg-event-ctx→reg-interceptor guidance),
;; and the frame-owned OBSERVABILITY-ROUTING E2E (a real dispatch routing
;; a projected handled-event / error record to a frame `:observability`
;; sink, registration-owned `:sensitive` event-arg redaction, fail-closed
;; routing) is owned END TO END by core's
;; `re-frame.observability-routing-cljs-test`. Those baseline scenarios are
;; NOT restated here.
;;
;; This tier is the ADVERSARIAL umbrella LOCK over the contracts that span
;; wider than either core suite: every assertion is shaped so a future
;; RE-INTRODUCTION of an old form (a working `reg-event-db`/`-fx`/`-ctx`),
;; a SECOND wrapper id, a re-appearing `:event/kind` sub-tag, or a
;; `reg-event-ctx` promotion back onto the public facade would turn it RED —
;; alongside the unique locks that have no in-core home (the canonical
;; coeffect shape, the closed effect-map negatives, the recordable-generator
;; / mint-policy triad, and the always-on error-/event-emit fan-out). It
;; lives in its own cross-artefact surface because the contract spans the
;; events runtime, the public facade, and the always-on error-/event-emit
;; channels.
;;
;; ## Why this deps.edn exists
;;
;; The conformance namespaces are `.cljc` and run in BOTH runtimes. They
;; ride the always-on CLJS `:node-test` gate (`npm run test:cljs`, ns
;; matches `cljs-test$`) via the cross-artefact source path the top-level
;; `implementation/shadow-cljs.edn` lists. This alias is the JVM
;; counterpart: it runs the SAME `.cljc` namespaces under the JVM so the
;; `:clj` reader-conditional arms (the `:no-doc`-meta facade probe, which
;; reads `(meta (var …))` and is JVM-only) AND the `:clj` host throw type
;; (`clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo`) are exercised — mirroring why
;; `reply-conformance/deps.edn` and `derivation-conformance/deps.edn`
;; exist. Wired into `scripts/test-jvm-implementation.sh`.
;;
;; ## Why test-only deps, not :local/root in :deps
;;
;; This artefact ships nothing, so the top-level `:deps` is empty. The
;; cross-artefact source the test namespaces `:require`
;; (`re-frame.core` — the public facade; plus the internal
;; `re-frame.events` / `re-frame.error-emit` / `re-frame.event-emit` /
;; `re-frame.registrar` / `re-frame.test-support` /
;; `re-frame.substrate.plain-atom` from core) is pulled in under the
;; `:test` alias only. `:extra-paths` is JUST `["test"]` so the cognitect
;; test-runner scans ONLY this tier's test dir — the `:local/root` core
;; dep contributes its `src` (never its `:test`), so core's own tests do
;; not run here.
;;
;; ## Bundle isolation (tools/README.md)
;;
;; No tool deps; this is a pure conformance surface. The dependency arrow
;; flows event-conformance(test) → core, never the reverse. Nothing under
;; `implementation/` production `src/` `:require`s anything here, so no
;; production bundle is widened.
{:paths []
 :deps  {}

 :aliases
 {:test
  {:extra-paths ["test"]
   ;; core carries the WHOLE one-form event contract: the public facade
   ;; (`re-frame.core`), the events runtime + retired stubs
   ;; (`re-frame.events`), the always-on error/event channels
   ;; (`re-frame.error-emit` / `re-frame.event-emit`), the registrar
   ;; (`re-frame.registrar`), the default substrate, and the shared test
   ;; harness.
   :extra-deps  {day8/re-frame2 {:local/root "../core"}
                 ;; rf2-try1x — silent-on-success reporter.
                 day8/re-frame2-test-quiet {:local/root "../test-quiet"}
                 io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner
                 {:git/tag "v0.5.1" :git/sha "dfb30dd"}}
   :main-opts   ["-m" "re-frame.test-quiet.runner"]}}}
